  "_uncertain_note": "The `uncertain` class is covered by TWO sentinels that share ONE word pair (counsel|council), and that is a measured limit rather than a choice. On the first dev-250 run every sentinel flip was an uncertain-class exemplar (sn-unc-03 three times in the same direction, sn-unc-02 once) — a reliably repeated non-expected answer is a defective exemplar, not drift. 15 replacement candidates were then probed against Terra across 5 structural patterns and 2 rounds (3 and 6 trials): possessive-number ambiguity, appositive/list scope, negation-scope commas, identifier-vs-typo, and real-word pairs. ONLY counsel|council held. Everything built to be 'structurally undecidable' — an unambiguous error with two meaning-distinct repairs — leaked into `meaning-damage` at 17-100%, and the reason is a gap in the prompt: it gives explicit tie-breaks for benign/unnecessary, unnecessary/damage and required/uncertain, but NONE for damage/uncertain, which are adjacent for exactly the cases that make a good uncertain exemplar. Adding that tie-break was rejected: it would resolve toward damage and make `uncertain` rarer still. Treat uncertain-class drift as covered by owner calibration, not by these two."
}
